# AI tool skill-pack auto-materializations under .agents/skills/
# Per OPERATOR_DECISION_MATRIX #25 closure 2026-05-25 PM cycle 2 - Option B (platform-wide).
# Targets the specific auto-materialization pattern (duplicate dirs under .agents/skills/<skill>/),
# NOT top-level .claude/.junie/.windsurf which IS tracked substrate content (e.g., .claude/PLATFORM/).
.agents/skills/**/.claude/
.agents/skills/**/.junie/
.agents/skills/**/.windsurf/

# Per-user editor + AI assistant local settings (NOT shared substrate)
# Per OPERATOR_DECISION_MATRIX #15 closure 2026-05-26 - track .claude/ framework substrate
# EXCEPT per-user state (permissions, local overrides).
.claude/settings.local.json

# Reference materials (PM schema substrate inputs + corpora; tracking not required per operator)
# Per OPERATOR_DECISION_MATRIX #64 closure 2026-05-26 - PM-Pro-Guide-xer-Templates (Primavera P6 XER
# sample corpus + Apr 2026 parser-output snapshots; informs matrix #19 PM Schema Foundation Plan
# but not part of code/commit substrate).
reference/*
# EXCEPT the canonical TCC Master Reference (the version-controlled single source of truth — must be tracked).
!reference/tcc/
# EXCEPT the records lane SSoT (charter, punch list, offline-sync rulings).
!reference/records/
# EXCEPT the Operations (PM) lane SSoT (re-baseline master index + chip specs).
!reference/ops/

# Audit workspace artifacts (read-only audit dispatches; never commit)
.audit_workspace/

# Local validation workspace (InvEq parity oracle, vendor binaries, decompiles —
# licensed third-party artifacts that must NEVER be committed). The reproducible
# outputs (captured-point fixtures) live under packages/*/tests/fixtures/ instead.
output/
infra/.env

# L6: allow the placeholder offsite-backup template (no secrets); real .env* stay ignored
!infra/backup/.env.dev-pg-offsite-backup.template

# uv: the root pyproject.toml is a bootstrap stub (not a [tool.uv.workspace]),
# so running uv at the repo root regenerates a trivial root lock as untracked
# noise. Ignore the root lock only (anchored) -- real per-package locks such
# as packages/apex-jobs/uv.lock stay tracked (apex-jobs has a real uv workspace).
# Deployers that build via requirements.txt (control-plane-api) and packages that
# are consumed as editable deps (learning-resolver) do NOT commit their lock files.
/uv.lock
apps/control-plane-api/uv.lock
packages/learning-resolver/uv.lock
packages/learning-capture/uv.lock

# real client estimator workbooks (never committed)
packages/ops-intake/_data/

# SDD controller scratch (subagent-driven-development progress ledger)
.superpowers/
